{
  "description": "The goal is to discover mixtures with low dynamic viscosity among the available mol_ids. Dynamic viscosity describes a fluid's resistance to flow. It matters when selecting mixtures for fluid handling, lubrication, or formulation.\n\nThe target is measured dynamic viscosity in centipoise (cP) at room temperature. The objective is to minimize dynamic viscosity. Lower values mean less resistance to flow.\n\nThe candidates are binary mixtures defined by two components and their mole fractions. The mole fractions specify the proportion of each component by amount of substance and sum to one. Both components have nonzero mole fractions.",
  "objective_convention": "y = dynamic viscosity in cP; minimize y.",
